    "name":  "Right testicular pain",
    "module":  "male-genital",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Right testicular pain refers to pain perceived in or around the right testicle, which may originate from the testis itself, the epididymis, the spermatic cord, or be referred from the lower abdomen or retroperitoneum. The most urgent cause to exclude is right testicular torsion — an emergency requiring surgical exploration within 6 hours to preserve testicular viability. Other causes include epididymo-orchitis, trauma, varicocele, hernia, and testicular tumour (which may present with a dull ache rather than acute pain).",
